class:: BeatLoudness
summary:: Beat-synchronous RMS and peak amplitude
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Rhythm
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Onsets2, Classes/BeatTrack3

description::
Accumulates squared samples and absolute peaks from one beat edge to the next. Reports the completed interval at the next edge; this is linear signal level, not psychoacoustic loudness or LUFS.

This is an independent implementation of the statistical definition above. Output updates at the server control rate; beat boundaries are quantized to a control block. Silence produces zero level/density or missing tempo evidence. No corpus-level accuracy is implied.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: in
Audio-rate mono signal to measure. Multichannel expansion creates independent analyzers.

argument:: beat
Control-rate beat trigger. Each rising edge completes the preceding interval and begins a new one.

argument:: maxInterval
Maximum beat interval in seconds, clipped to 0.1–60, default 10. Expired results reset to zero.

returns::
[linearRMS, linearPeak], initially zero until a complete beat interval.

examples::
The sample is rhythmically gated to give the estimator repeatable attacks. Analysis drives the filtering, panning or second synthesized voice. Allow a few seconds for tempo acquisition.
code::
(
Routine({
    var buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2RhythmExample = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, buffer, BufRateScale.kr(buffer), loop: 1)
            * Decay2.kr(Impulse.kr(2), 0.005, 0.12);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(2048), source, 0.25);
        var onset = Onsets2.kr(chain, threshold: 0.15, fftSize: 2048, hop: 0.25);
        var level = BeatLoudness.kr(source, onset[0]);
        var sound = [source * 0.25, SinOsc.ar(440, 0, level[0].lag(0.03) * 0.3)];
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;
    ~mir2RhythmBuffer = buffer;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::

Stop and release:
code::
(
~mir2RhythmExample.free;
~mir2RhythmBuffer.free;
)
::

